# Task 14: PHONE CALLING: DECISIONS AND THREAT MODEL -- DESIGN ONLY (priority: medium)
# Depends on: 11 closed. Gate: nothing from 15 onward starts until I approve this.
#docs/phone-calls-design @hargrove: This is task 14 in Tasks.herd. You lead the threat model. Whether this is worth doing is a priority call for me and Kai, so set out the options and do not decide it. You're working in lordmuffin/jarvis-voice. Read PR #44 and its code, docs/designs/voice-talkback.md, the approved-action work from task 4 (docs/plans/copilot-actions.md) and server/deploy/README.md. Output docs/designs/phone-calls.md. No production code. END THE DOC with open questions for me. Goal: decide what Jarvis placing a real phone call is for, and what must be true before it may ring anyone. Context you can trust: PR #44 is 403+ commits stale, in legacy src/jarvis_voice/ (bugfix only), against a dead listener and a decommissioned proxy. It has no auth on any /calls route and no Twilio signature check. gTTS sends call text to Google. Worth keeping: the mu-law conversion, the Media Streams flow, the [CALL_COMPLETE] signal. Recommend closing it; closing is my call. Cover: - The real use cases, ranked, and the smallest one worth building. If there is no recurring use, say so; "don't build it" is a valid outcome. - Carrier: Twilio vs a SIP trunk into the existing Asterisk box. That box is an intercom today and no phone-network trunk is configured, so either way a carrier is needed and telephony cannot run on the Spark. - Threat model: who can place a call, toll fraud, webhook forgery, prompt injection by the person on the line, transcript exposure, and the single most damaging failure. Rate findings critical/high/medium/low, blockers separate. - Authorisation: every outbound call is a task 4 style PROPOSAL I approve, with number, purpose and limits. No autonomous dialling. - Legal: AI-voice call rules (FCC/TCPA), state call recording and transcription consent, disclosure that the caller is an AI. Cite sources. If it needs a real lawyer's view, say that and do not guess. - Local-only (task 6): how a work or ambiguous call is refused or kept off the homelab. Where third-party call audio is stored and for how long. - Which lab and live rules apply: credentials on each channel, and whether lab gets dialling at all. Constraints: Hargrove rates and names risks, the decisions stay mine. DONE WHEN: I approve the design, or we decide not to build and park tasks 15-20.

